# Backend Architecture

The backend system is built using Flask with Socket.IO integration to provide real-time communication between the frontend and the LangGraph MCP agent.

## Main Components

- [backend/app.py](mdc:backend/app.py) - Core Flask application with Socket.IO setup
- [client.py](mdc:client.py) - Client utility for connecting to the backend
- [lambda_client.py](mdc:lambda_client.py) - Lambda client implementation
- [lambda_client_adapter.py](mdc:lambda_client_adapter.py) - Adapter for the lambda client

## Agent Implementation

- [src/agent/client.py](mdc:src/agent/client.py) - MCP agent client implementation

## MCP Servers

- [src/mcp_servers/math_server.py](mdc:src/mcp_servers/math_server.py) - Server for handling math queries
- [src/mcp_servers/weather_server.py](mdc:src/mcp_servers/weather_server.py) - Server for handling weather queries

## Key Dependencies

The backend requires the following key packages:
- Flask
- Flask-SocketIO
- LangGraph
- Other dependencies listed in [requirements.txt](mdc:requirements.txt)
